## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-time multi-tenant deployment, latency budgets, privacy guarantees, and drift monitoring in production-like settings.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time multi-tenant inference
- Early-exit and mixed-precision optimization
- DP/FL privacy guarantees and secure aggregation
- Drift detection and rollout strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference skeleton for two-tower model
function twoTowerInfer(input, tenantId, model) {
  // shared backbone
  const shared = model.backbone.extract(input.features)
  // tenant-specific embedding
  const emb = model.tenantEmbeddings[tenantId](input.userId)
  // combine and head with early exit
  const fused = concatenate(shared, emb)
  return model.heads[0](fused) // early exit path
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to handle new tenants with cold-start data? 
- How to quantify privacy-utility trade-offs with DP/Secure Aggregation?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design scalable, tenant-aware ML pipelines with calibration, streaming features, drift handling, and safe rollout strategies across enterprise-scale tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant feature stores and leakage prevention
- Shared base model + per-tenant calibrator
- Real-time features from streaming usage and billing
- Online retraining with drift detectors
- Offline + online evaluation and staged rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo calibration hook
function calibrate(probs, tenantId, store){
  const params = store.getParams(tenantId)
  // adjust by temp scaler
  return Math.min(0.999, Math.max(0.001, probs * params.scale + params.bias))
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant calibration offline and online?
- How would you guard against cross-tenant data leakage in CV and feature drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical NLP pipeline setup, handling class imbalance, and real-world deployment concerns for a beginner-friendly problem.

## Key Concepts
- TF-IDF vectorization with unigrams/bigrams
- Handling imbalanced data via class_weight
- Time-based train/test splits to mimic streaming data
- Evaluation: macro F1 and PR-AUC for imbalanced tasks
- Canary rollout and monitoring basics for production safety

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: outline of pipeline components
function buildPipeline(){
  const vectorizer = new TFIDF({ngramRange:[1,2], maxFeatures:100000});
  const model = new LogisticRegression({classWeight:'balanced'});
  return {vectorizer, model};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to multi-class categorization of spam types?
- How would you monitor drift and adjust thresholds in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests on-device ML design under strict latency, privacy, and fairness constraints; requires end-to-end thinking from data flow to deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Edge ML and latency budgets
- Federated learning with DP
